    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Connect your form\n\nPoint your form's webhook at this node's URL (**POST**):\n- Typeform: Connect > Webhooks.\n- Tally: Integrations > Webhooks.\n- Your landing page: POST with `Content-Type: application/json`.\n\nThe whole `body` goes to Claude (cut at 8,000 characters), so it works with any of them.",
        "height": 312,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        1000
      ],
      "id": "c7aa70f3-ddf7-4ffc-a4d0-c6fdd7d03a3f",
      "name": "Setup 1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Claude\n\n*Claude model*, Credential, paste your **Anthropic API key**. Default: **Haiku 4.5**.\n\nIt returns `summary`, `intent` and `priority`.",
        "height": 228,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        310,
        1000
      ],
      "id": "3f5fabcb-981b-45a8-90f5-0e417e9b09bd",
      "name": "Setup 2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Sheets and Slack\n\n**Sheets:** connect Google, pick the document and the sheet, automatic mapping. Headers: **summary, intent, priority, received_at**.\n\n**Slack:** create an *Incoming Webhook* in your workspace and paste its URL in *Post to Slack*. The URL is the credential: keep it out of screenshots and shared exports.\n\nThe Slack body is built with `JSON.stringify`, so quotes or line breaks in the summary cannot break the JSON.",
        "height": 396,
        "width": 320,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        1000
      ],
      "id": "2e5caab7-b03a-41d5-980e-d53eaab33731",
      "name": "Setup 3"
    }
